    "statute": "Cal. Veh. Code \u00a711713.1(e); 13 CCR \u00a7262",
    "recommendation": "**NEEDS HUMAN REVIEW AND VERIFICATION** \u2014 California requires an advertised vehicle price to be available to any member of the public, and conditional incentives (loyalty, conquest, military, college grad, captive-finance credits) may only be deducted from an advertised price if the qualification is clearly disclosed. This footer states pricing \"includes all offers and incentives\" without naming a single incentive or its qualification, and the BMW offers elsewhere on the site are expressly conditional (\"Loyalty Offers available to qualified customers who have leased or financed a BMW model through BMW Financial Services NA, LLC in the last 12 months\", \"Must finance through BMW Financial Services\"). Itemize the incentives included in the advertised price and state their qualification conditions, or advertise the price available to all buyers with conditional incentives shown as separate potential deductions.",
    "confidence": "medium",
    "needs_human_review": true
  },
